An opt-in `--inlined-body-call-permissions` option makes a precondition that calls a recursive predicate on a constructed value, such as `t.scoped(|s|)` for `t := Bin(op, Var(0), Var(1))` where `scoped` is `a.scoped(n) && b.scoped(n)` on `Bin`, provable independently of the surrounding declarations: each separately checked conjunct of the inlined body gets the body's call permissions at its own fuel layer, an instance of the existing definition axiom (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/198). Without it, the second conjunct is proved only when some unrelated term happens to unfold the first, so which of two equivalent declarations fails moves with declaration order. It has its own option, not `--additional-axioms`, because it changes proof costs; it is disabled by default.
